{# The work surface of the app. A screen puts exactly ONE of these into the
   shell's `content` slot, and this template is the only place the relation
   between a screen's header, its filters, its main region and its inspector is
   written down: `header` spans the full width, and below it a row places
   `filters` on the leading edge (192px, `w-48` on Tailwind's 4px-based dynamic
   spacing scale — 48 × 4px), `main` (the flexible remainder) and `inspector`
   (320px, `w-80`), single column below `lg`.

   EACH ASIDE DROPS OUT OF THE TEMPLATE when its slot is empty, rather than
   rendering an empty 192px or 320px gutter. Its content is CAPTURED first, so
   the test is what the region actually renders — a slot filled through a
   `{% block %}` override carries no variable of that name, and testing the
   variable would drop a region that has content.

   THE ROW IS FLEX, NOT A CSS GRID TEMPLATE. Fixed-width asides sized with a
   `grid-template-columns` literal (`192px minmax(0,1fr) 320px`) can only be
   written as an arbitrary-value Tailwind class, which the token-discipline
   gate (BB-504) forbids in a layout component same as anywhere else. A
   flex row states the same three tracks with named-scale utilities instead:
   each aside carries `w-48`/`w-80` and `shrink-0`, `main` carries `flex-1`, and
   the single-column collapse below `lg` is `flex-col` reverting to `flex-row`
   at `lg` rather than a grid template swap — the aside widths apply only from
   `lg` up (`lg:w-48`/`lg:w-80`), so a narrow viewport gets full-width stacked
   regions in document order exactly as it did before.

   `main` is not conditional. It is the region that carries the route, so a
   canvas without it is a screen without a subject, and an author who forgot to
   fill it should see an empty main column rather than a silently reflowed grid.

   THIS IS NOT A SCROLL CONTAINER, and must never become one. `items-start`
   keeps the flex items at their natural height, and no clipping declaration
   appears anywhere in this file — a scrolling ancestor here would take the
   sticky `inspector` and the sticky `filters` their stick, and an absolutely
   positioned picker panel (a `meta_row`'s inline edit, a facet control) cannot
   escape one, so it would be cut off at the region's edge instead of opening
   over it (D6, D12, BB-332 R9).

   BOTH ASIDES STICK FROM THEIR OWN FLEX ITEM, and that placement — not the
   declaration itself — is the whole of why they stick. A sticky flex item is
   offset inside its own flex line, which with `items-start` is as tall as
   itself — a `self-start` on the item and `items-start` on the row are what
   let the item's containing block be tall enough to give the `sticky` a
   travel range, exactly as the grid version needed the item to sit in the
   full-height GRID AREA rather than a cell shrunk to its content. This is
   the same fix `inspector` needed until BB-414 measured it stuck at
   zero travel range; `filters` never had the bug because it was written this
   way from the start. `inspector.twig`'s own <aside> still declares a `sticky
   top-0`, which inside this row is inert for exactly the reason above; it is
   left standing because the component answers for itself wherever else it is
   placed, and it is not what makes the rail stick here. The remedy for a rail
   that does not stick is never a clipping declaration on this element or any
   ancestor of it — the A6 contract check greps this file for the property
   that does it, and is right to — because that would buy the stick back at
   the price of the paragraph above.

   Spacing is the token scale, never a hard pixel value: the gap between the
   header and the row, and between the row's tracks, is `space-5` (D16).

   `main` is a vertical flex stack with the same `space-5` gap, so the region
   owns the rhythm between its children; a single child still stretches to the
   full width. `inspector` uses the same `flex flex-col gap-5` stack, so two
   surface panels in that region keep the canvas rhythm instead of sitting
   flush. Inspector asides are `w-full` so a short panel still fills the
   320px column.

   THE STICKY `filters` ASIDE CARRIES A `z-index`, AND THAT IS NOT DECORATION.
   `position: sticky` creates a stacking context whatever its `z-index` — so
   every absolutely positioned panel a facet control opens is trapped inside the
   aside's own stacking context and cannot paint over its siblings. `main`'s
   table has positioned cells (`<td class="relative">`) that come LATER in the
   document, so with the aside at `z-index: auto` they painted on top of the
   panel: `document.elementFromPoint()` at the centre of an open facet row
   returned that `<td>` and a pointer click picked nothing, while focus and Space
   on the row's own control still worked. The fix is the `z-index` and not
   `position: static` and not `overflow`: static would cost the aside its stick,
   and a clipping declaration is forbidden two paragraphs above, because a facet
   opened low in a long list must be able to open past the aside's own bottom
   edge. `40` places the aside above the content row and below `dialog`'s `50`,
   which is the theme's existing scale (BB-413 R8).
   The whole declaration is `lg:`-gated because the stick is: below `lg` the
   aside is static, creates no stacking context, and the panel's own `z-30`
   already paints over the table. #}
{% set header_content %}{% block header %}{{ header }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set filters_content %}{% block filters %}{{ filters }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set main_content %}{% block main %}{{ main }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set inspector_content %}{% block inspector %}{{ inspector }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set has_filters = filters_content|trim is not empty %}
{% set has_inspector = inspector_content|trim is not empty %}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['flex', 'flex-col', 'gap-5']) }}>
  {% if header_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div data-canvas-region="header">{{ header_content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-5 items-start px-5 pb-5 {{ header_content|trim is empty ? 'pt-5' : '' }}">
    {% if has_filters %}
      <div data-canvas-region="filters" class="w-full lg:w-48 lg:shrink-0 min-w-0 self-start lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:z-40">{{ filters_content }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    <div data-canvas-region="main" class="w-full lg:w-auto flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-5">{{ main_content }}</div>
    {% if has_inspector %}
      <div data-canvas-region="inspector" class="w-full lg:w-80 lg:shrink-0 min-w-0 self-start lg:sticky lg:top-0 flex flex-col gap-5">{{ inspector_content }}</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
